%% Data come either from the Operator in the app or, «planned», from the simulated farm devices and cameras through one common data channel (no
%% hardware). Alerts in v1.4: Mortality from box events, MilestoneDelay and DataSilence from the alert job, EvidenceFlag from an expired capture request.
%% The cycle repeats every day until harvest (WF-04). Connector A continues on part 2. Evidence states (Figure 4.28): risk < 20 Accepted; Watch goes
%% straight to the Evidence Reviewer; Flagged evidence may get the Operator's explanation first; a NeedMoreEvidence verdict makes it Flagged again. The
%% crab detection module only checks that a crab is present and adds to the risk score (develop runs a no-op detector); a person decides. Rejected
%% evidence notifies the Operator. The Investor's view of own box details is a separate flow: it reads the accepted evidence and box data at any time.
%% Connector B continues on part 3. Milestone gate (Figure 4.13): tranche 1 needs the capital closed and contracts signed; later tranches need stocking
%% and accepted evidence since the last tranche with none flagged; tranche 3 or later needs a declared harvest date. Release creates a disbursement
%% instruction (Figure 4.12) that the Administrator sends; after an explanation the Operator requests the tranche again (no direct release); a blocked
%% tranche stops the later ones. Traceability: UC17, UC52, UC19, UC20, UC45, UC47, UC48, UC21, UC53, UC18, UC40 (TP4 Khôi; ingestion and simulator TP2
%% Viên; disbursement TP1 Thiện). Precondition: capital closed and every contract FullySigned (WF-02); only the boxes of funded rows are stocked.
%% Exception branches: mortality over the limit, alert not acknowledged in time (escalated), watch or flagged evidence reviewed by a person, rejected
%% evidence, more evidence requested, tranche request refused, explanation requested, tranche blocked. «planned» in v1.4: the simulated farm devices and
%% cameras with one common data channel, the trained crab detection module, box rows and row-scoped box details for investors. Removed in v1.4 (still in
%% code): per-crab tags and tag photos; WaterQuality alerts with the water thresholds and readings of daily logs (pH, temperature, salinity). States:
%% Batch Stocked → InProduction (Figure 4.8); alert Open → Acknowledged / Escalated → Resolved (4.30); capture request Open → Fulfilled / Expired (4.29);
%% evidence Accepted / Watch / Flagged / Rejected (4.28); tranche Planned → Requested → Released / NeedsExplanation / Blocked (4.13). Design decisions of
